---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Safety & Self-defence — Women Safety" description="Awareness, escape planning and responsible self-defence guidance.">
  <section class="hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Women Safety</p><h1>Safety & Self-defence</h1><p class="lead">The goal of self-defence is awareness, creating an opportunity to get away and reaching help—not winning a fight.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container grid-3">
    <article class="card"><h2>Awareness</h2><p class="muted">Notice exits, staffed areas, security points and changes in your surroundings. Trust warning signs and move toward safety early.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h2>Safety planning</h2><p class="muted">Keep trusted contacts, a charged phone, important information and a safe destination in mind before you need them.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h2>Get training</h2><p class="muted">Consider a reputable self-defence or martial-arts class with qualified instructors and a safe, practical training environment.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h2>Useful skills</h2><ul class="feature-list"><li>Early-risk recognition</li><li>Clear verbal boundaries</li><li>Creating distance</li><li>Moving toward exits and people</li><li>Calling for help quickly</li></ul></article>
    <article class="card"><h2>Martial arts</h2><p class="muted">Boxing, judo, karate, taekwondo, Brazilian jiu-jitsu and other disciplines can support fitness, coordination and controlled practice. Choose a safe instructor and training environment.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h2>Remember</h2><p class="muted">No technique guarantees safety. When escape is possible, getting away and reaching other people is the priority.</p></article>
  </div></section>
</Layout>